# InKognito (Bigme B1051C Pro): first-boot provisioning of the e-ink layer. Installed as /system/etc/init/inkognito.rc.
# The scripts run in Magisk's SELinux domain, so they need the release's Magisk-patched boot.img; without it the
# exec fails and Android boots plain. Both scripts exit at once when their marker exists, so later boots cost nothing.
#
# Boot 1 (fresh /data): zygote-start runs after every post-fs-data action (Magisk's included) and before "boot",
# which starts SurfaceFlinger and TrebleDroid's phh-su daemon. Stage 1 installs the Magisk modules there and
# reboots, so the panel never shows an unshimmed frame and AOSP Provision never runs.
on zygote-start
    exec u:r:magisk:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/etc/inkognito/provision-stage1.sh

# Boot 2: install and configure the apps while Google setup is on screen.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    exec_background u:r:magisk:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/etc/inkognito/provision-stage2.sh
